 "dur": 45.0,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Why did a dog named Bobbie walk 2,500 miles through winter?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.57
  },
  {
   "text": "Six months after he vanished, a skinny collie scratches at a door in Oregon.",
   "s": 3.87,
   "e": 7.674
  },
  {
   "text": "But Bobbie got lost in Indiana, on the other side of America.",
   "s": 7.874,
   "e": 11.09
  },
  {
   "text": "If it's him, he crossed rivers, deserts and the Rocky Mountains alone.",
   "s": 11.29,
   "e": 14.699
  },
  {
   "text": "The neighbors laugh. No dog finds home from Indiana.",
   "s": 14.899,
   "e": 17.639
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the letters start arriving, from people who fed him on the way.",
   "s": 17.839,
   "e": 20.891
  },
  {
   "text": "A farmer in Iowa. A cook in Wyoming. A family who hid him from a blizzard.",
   "s": 21.091,
   "e": 25.225
  },
  {
   "text": "He swam an icy river and climbed mountains buried in snow.",
   "s": 25.425,
   "e": 28.398
  },
  {
   "text": "So how did he know the way? He retraced the family's road trip, town by town.",
   "s": 28.798,
   "e": 32.718
  },
  {
   "text": "Then Oregon goes wild: medals, keys to cities, and his own little house.",
   "s": 32.918,
   "e": 36.29
  },
  {
   "text": "Forty thousand people line up to pet him.",
   "s": 36.49,
   "e": 38.401
  },
  {
   "text": "He even stars as himself in a movie.",
   "s": 38.601,
   "e": 40.349
  },
  {
   "text": "2,500 miles, all to scratch at one door.",
   "s": 40.549,
   "e": 43.418
  }
 ],
